{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"**Selection:** The trust’s board selects the independent auditor for the relevant series, through an in-person vote of a majority of directors who are not “interested persons.” An audit committee’s recommendation does not replace that statutory vote. See [Investment Company Act §32(a)](https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/15/80a-31).\n\n**Shareholder ratification may be omitted when:**\n- **No annual shareholder meeting is held.** Section 32(a)(2) requires submission at the next annual meeting, “if any”; it does not require convening one solely for auditor ratification.\n- **Rule 32a-4 applies—even if an annual meeting occurs.** The board must establish an entirely non-interested-director audit committee; the committee must adopt a written charter; and the trust must satisfy charter and committee-minute retention requirements. See [Rule 32a-4](https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/17/270.32a-4).\n\n**Worth knowing:** The exemption removes shareholder ratification—not independent-director selection."}}
